<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      Notifications PR6 — the service-scoped mod-action COMMS directive rides the
      mod_action row.

      A moderator can ask the platform to NOTIFY the affected user about a ban/lift/lock
      via the per-domain neutral @system sender. The DIRECTIVE (which channels; or
      email-only) is recorded on the action row so it is auditable + can be forwarded to
      admin-bff's notification subsystem. Two NULLABLE columns (null on every legacy row
      + when the mod requests no notification):

        - notify_channels    a CSV of requested channel names (e.g. 'in-app,matrix'),
                             SERVICE-SCOPED by the action's platform (a 'matrix' ban can
                             request the matrix channel; an unrelated channel is dropped
                             by the service before it is stored). NULL = no directive.
        - notify_email_only  when true, the directive is forced to email + in-app ONLY
                             (the conservative low-noise option) regardless of
                             notify_channels. NULL/false = honour notify_channels.

      CRITICAL IDENTITY RULE: these columns DESCRIBE the requested fan-out; they NEVER
      carry — and the @system outbox-builder in admin-bff NEVER copies — the acting
      mod identity (mod_action.actor). The neutral @system sender must never expose who
      moderated (the same posture as the public AppealContact resolver).

      SHIPS DARK: nothing consumes these columns yet beyond the audit row + the
      forwarded directive; admin-bff's outbox subsystem (PR2/PR5/PR7) is the consumer.

      Numbered 008, one above the current max (007-mod-action-wiki). Portable addColumn
      (PostgreSQL + the H2 PostgreSQL-compat test store). Appended LAST in the master.
    -->

    <changeSet id="008-mod-action-notify-columns" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>Add the service-scoped @system notification directive columns to
                 mod_action: notify_channels (CSV) + notify_email_only (bool). Both
                 nullable — null on legacy rows + when no notification is requested.
                 NEVER carries the acting mod identity.</comment>
        <addColumn tableName="mod_action">
            <!-- CSV of requested channels, service-scoped by platform. NULL = none. -->
            <column name="notify_channels" type="varchar(256)"/>
            <!-- Force email + in-app only when true. NULL/false = honour notify_channels. -->
            <column name="notify_email_only" type="boolean"/>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
